{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_n4nvs6e3cknu5gltjd3xecydmhuscfwtx4p4qgmk4igxxi2su2fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 8 integration tests pass. The Rust translation produces byte-identical output to the C library across many input combinations including edge cases (zero, negatives, the special `x==1 && y==4` case that triggers `goto label2`, and a 6×6 input grid).\n\nSummary:\n- **Cargo.toml**: cdylib crate-type, libc dependency for `printf`, libloading dev-dependency.\n- **src/lib.rs**: Translates the `driver(int x, int y)` C function preserving its `goto`-based control flow exactly. The C uses a `while` loop with two labels (`label1`, `label2`) — `label2` skips the x-decrement block on the special `x==1 && y==4` trigger, and `goto label1` from inside is reached after `y--` when `x < 3`. I unrolled this into structured Rust with an inner loop that mirrors the goto chain.\n- **tests/ffi_compare.rs**: Loads both `libdriver.so` (C) and `target/release/libdriver.so` (Rust) via `libloading`, redirects fd 1 with `dup`/`dup2` around each call to capture printf output, and compares byte-for-byte.\n- Symbol parity verified via `nm -D`: both libraries export `driver` as the only `T` symbol."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":518,"cache_read_input_tokens":21405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":518,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7dc753a-e3cd-4bf8-8469-7e4718f73f8f","uuid":"b87b64f0-33b3-4599-bd0a-b8049517db87"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":137660,"duration_api_ms":133871,"ttft_ms":2202,"num_turns":16,"result":"All 8 integration tests pass. The Rust translation produces byte-identical output to the C library across many input combinations including edge cases (zero, negatives, the special `x==1 && y==4` case that triggers `goto label2`, and a 6×6 input grid).\n\nSummary:\n- **Cargo.toml**: cdylib crate-type, libc dependency for `printf`, libloading dev-dependency.\n- **src/lib.rs**: Translates the `driver(int x, int y)` C function preserving its `goto`-based control flow exactly. The C uses a `while` loop with two labels (`label1`, `label2`) — `label2` skips the x-decrement block on the special `x==1 && y==4` trigger, and `goto label1` from inside is reached after `y--` when `x < 3`. I unrolled this into structured Rust with an inner loop that mirrors the goto chain.\n- **tests/ffi_compare.rs**: Loads both `libdriver.so` (C) and `target/release/libdriver.so` (Rust) via `libloading`, redirects fd 1 with `dup`/`dup2` around each call to capture printf output, and compares byte-for-byte.\n- Symbol parity verified via `nm -D`: both libraries export `driver` as the only `T` symbol.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f7dc753a-e3cd-4bf8-8469-7e4718f73f8f","total_cost_usd":0.52597725,"usage":{"input_tokens":20,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8559,"cache_read_input_tokens":267517,"output_tokens":13545,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8559},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7[1m]":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":13545,"cacheReadInputTokens":267517,"cacheCreationInputTokens":8559,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.52597725,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"comple